<BaseLayout title="stenbom.me" description="About Robert Stenbom.">
	<h1>Robert Stenbom</h1>
	<p>
		I'm Robert. I've been writing code for over 20 years, and this year marks 20 years of doing it professionally. I'm currently chief architect at <a href="https://www.ingrid.com/">Ingrid</a>, a role I started at the beginning of 2025.
	</p>
	<p>
		Before that I spent about ten years as a CTO across two companies. The first was Advinans, which got acquired by Nordea and became <a href="https://nordeanode.se/">Nordea Node</a>. I stayed there for around seven years, watching a small company turn into part of a bank.
	</p>
	<p>
		This site is mostly a technical blog. I like writing from time to time, not because anyone asked, but because it's a good way to work out what I actually think about something. If a post turns out useful to someone else too, that's a bonus.
	</p>
	<p>
		You can find my code on <a href="https://github.com/TransitoryBliss">GitHub</a>, or read the <a href="/blog/">blog</a>.
	</p>
</BaseLayout>
